cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "deposit.mayday.software"
message: >-
  Signed, timestamped authorship attestation for the deposit.mayday.software website.
  Verify the detached SSH signature (CITATION.cff.sig, namespace "file") against the
  published public key (signing-key.pub, a hardware key) to prove WHO, and the
  OpenTimestamps proof (CITATION.cff.ots) to prove WHEN. Verify locally at
  https://deposit.mayday.software/authorship — files never leave your browser — or
  with ssh-keygen -Y check-novalidate -n file -f signing-key.pub -s CITATION.cff.sig < CITATION.cff
abstract: >-
  deposit — open-source cryptographic copyright deposit: files are hashed in the
  browser and the proof is anchored in Bitcoin (OpenTimestamps) and RFC 3161
  timestamping authorities. This file is a cryptographic authorship attestation,
  not the source: the signature proves it was issued by Ilia Arestov
  (code@ilia.ae) and the OpenTimestamps anchor proves the date.
authors:
  - given-names: Ilia
    family-names: Arestov
    email: code@ilia.ae
url: "https://deposit.mayday.software"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ilia-ae/deposit.mayday.software"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-07"
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - deposit
  - authorship
  - attestation
  - ssh-signature
  - opentimestamps
  - sha256
